## Hero Map Terrain

`public/data/world-relief.json` holds a global elevation grid. The hero glyph
map reads it. `scripts/bake-world-map.mjs` generates it.

The elevations come from the NOAA ETOPO1 Global Relief Model. That model is a
work of the United States government and is in the public domain.

    https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/etopo-global-relief-model

The grid derives from a baked tile in the glyphcss repository, at
`website/public/data/flatmap/0/0_0.json`. The bake script reads that tile,
drops the surfaces the hero never renders, and rewrites the rest as a grid.

    https://github.com/apresmoi/glyphcss

